# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code visual-iteration sandbox env (Vite `--mode sandbox`).
#
# Loaded automatically by `npm run dev:sandbox` / `npm run tauri:dev:sandbox`.
# Copy this file to `.env.sandbox.local` (gitignored) to activate.
#
# This sandbox is for Claude Code only. The user's personal dev wallet
# runs on the main `npm run tauri dev` instance and must never be
# touched by Claude. See CLAUDE.md § "Isolated Dev Iteration Sandbox".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Skip the vault unlock screen on mount so the dashboard renders without
# typing a password. Same flag the main dev-bypass uses.
VITE_SKIP_AUTH=true

# Selects which scenario the src/lib/tauri.ts mock invoke returns.
# Available values:
#   idle                 — miners detected, nothing running. Default.
#   mining_projected     — CPU XMR session AND a funded wallet. The fixture for
#                          the Mine tab's SIMPLE hero (canvas frame 3a): the
#                          projected balance needs a mined XMR BALANCE and
#                          prices, and mining_active_24hr deliberately has
#                          neither, so that scenario can only render the `—`
#                          branch. Added 2026-08-28 with workstream 7.
#   mining_active_24hr   — active CPU mining session, 24h history with
#                          one drop-to-zero segment + one spike, 1 worker.
#   gpu_mining_active    — active GPU session (Ergo/Autolykos2, ~115 MH/s)
#                          with the activeSessions store seeded, so the
#                          post-reload rehydration path renders the GPU
#                          running hero on load (webview2 Round 13 fix).
#   cpu_gpu_mining_active — CONCURRENT lanes: Zephyr on CPU (~7.3 kH/s) +
#                          Ergo on GPU (~115 MH/s), both descriptors seeded.
#                          Reproduces the post-reload per-hardware-coin bug
#                          (CPU must show Zephyr, GPU must show Ergo) and the
#                          per-lane gating / landscape hardware toggle.
#   wallet_populated     — funded multi-chain wallet: real balances for every
#                          chain + populated Activity + active XMR/ZPH
#                          (portfolio ≈ $16.9k). Verifies the wallet / activity
#                          / privacy surface. See sandbox-demo-mode-improvements.
#   degraded             — funded, but prices 503 + ETH-mainnet RPC errors +
#                          unhealthy mining: verifies data-absent affordances
#                          (— not $0, per-chain error isolation).
#   swap_sidecar_idle    — funded wallet, BasicSwap sidecar OPTED IN but the
#                          node is STOPPED. Drives SidecarStatusCard's stopped
#                          branch and a start from Settings: swap_sidecar_start
#                          steps preparing -> starting -> healthy over ~3s, and
#                          any /json/* call before healthy fails with the
#                          backend's own "the swap node is not running".
#   swap_sidecar_active  — funded wallet, node HEALTHY, offer book populated
#                          (7 resting offers laddered +0.2% / +1.4% / +3.2% /
#                          +7.8% / +14.2% off the sandbox market mid, so the
#                          spread gate's green, amber AND red-block bands are
#                          all reachable), plus ONE in-flight swap sitting
#                          mid-protocol at BidState 11 ("Scriptless coin
#                          locked" -> "Waiting for counterparty").
#                          Particl reports SYNCED here (blocks == headers, at
#                          verifiedPct 99.99982 — the trailing nines a real
#                          caught-up daemon actually returns), because "offer
#                          book populated" and "chain 1.9M blocks behind" cannot
#                          both be true. Before 2026-08-28 this scenario shipped
#                          a 13.73% Particl, which made the swap-node card's
#                          `PART 100%` branch unreachable in the sandbox and hid
#                          a bug where a synced node read 99% forever.
#   swap_sidecar_stuck   — same as swap_sidecar_active, but Particl is MID-SYNC
#                          (13.73%, 349,745 of 2,226,731 blocks), which is what
#                          makes the swap-node card's warn tone reachable. NOTE:
#                          the older comment on this fixture claimed it existed
#                          "so the sync bar renders in a browser run" — that was
#                          never true. `DexParticlCard`, the component with the
#                          sync bar, is exported from the swap-sidecar barrel and
#                          covered by syncState.test.ts but MOUNTED NOWHERE, so no
#                          browser run has ever rendered it. Checked 2026-08-28:
#                          `grep -rn "<DexParticlCard" src/` returns nothing.
#                          And the in-flight bid
#                          sits at BidState 23 (BID_ERROR, "Bid error, check
#                          events for details"). This is the ONLY scenario that
#                          reaches SidecarSwapTracker's RecoveryPanel — the
#                          "Restart this swap" affordance for the one stage the
#                          engine never resumes on its own. Reproduces the
#                          2026-08-23 mainnet incident. swap_sidecar_recover_bid
#                          returns recovered:true here and a REFUSAL (with a
#                          reason) in every other scenario, so both branches of
#                          the UI are reachable.
#                          NOTE: the swap-sidecar-progress event cannot fire in
#                          browser-only mode (no Tauri event bus), so the setup
#                          wizard shows its phase-poll fallback here; the real
#                          progress meter needs `npm run tauri:dev:sandbox`.
VITE_MOCK_STATE=mining_active_24hr

# Marks this Vite instance as the dev sandbox so the invoke wrapper
# returns mocks instead of throwing when the Tauri runtime is absent
# (i.e. when running pure `npm run dev:sandbox` in a browser).
VITE_DEV_INSTANCE=sandbox

# ── Optional sandbox knobs (sandbox-demo-mode-improvements plan) ──────────
#
# Tier C — set to `real` to DISABLE the window.fetch shim so the BIP39 test
# seed hits real read-only RPCs (real on-chain data; the test seed is
# world-public, so there's nothing to steal). Unset / anything else = mocked.
# VITE_SANDBOX_NETWORK=real
#
# Force a specific pre-vault / onboarding view on boot (the VITE_SKIP_AUTH
# bypass otherwise jumps straight to the dashboard). Dev-only. Any view id,
# e.g. home | login | import | backup | setPassword | derivation-picker.
# VITE_FORCE_VIEW=import
#
# Device profile for cpuInfo()/gpuInfo(): default | no-gpu | low-end | multi-gpu.
# Exercises DeviceProfilePanel + the miner-recommendation branches.
# VITE_MOCK_DEVICE=no-gpu

# Pretend an app update is available, so the startup UpdateBanner can be seen.
# The real check needs the Tauri runtime and can never fire under dev:sandbox,
# which is how the app shipped an updater nobody had watched render. Set to the
# version to advertise. Dev-only (dead-code-eliminated from `vite build`).
# VITE_MOCK_UPDATE=0.7.0

# ── Swap routing flags ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Mirror of the same keys in .env.local — see that file for the full
# rationale. Set both to `true` to keep the sandbox UI in sync with
# the main wallet's post-cutover treatment. The sandbox's invoke
# calls are mocked via tauri-mocks.ts regardless of these flags, so
# they only affect UI banner state and the MockSwapAttemptedError
# broadcast hard-stop (which fires defensively if a sandbox scenario
# ever exercises a real swap path).
VITE_SWAPKIT_LIVE=true
VITE_SWAPKIT_CANARY=true
#
#   utxo_change_stranded
#     Reproduces the 2026-08-22 mainnet incident on the sandbox test seed:
#     the DISPLAYED Litecoin address has history but is empty (funded, then
#     spent), and 4.02888049 LTC sits on the change chain at index 20 -- one
#     past BIP-44's standard gap limit of 20. Use it to verify that the
#     account scan finds change the single-address model missed, and that the
#     restore-safety warning on the account-addresses card renders with a
#     required gap limit of 21. The only scenario where per-address balance
#     answers differ from each other.
#
#     Since 2026-08-25 it also mocks per-address UTXO SETS, not just balances,
#     so the SPEND path is exercisable: sending 1.0 LTC while the displayed
#     address holds 0.00000000 must succeed by reaching the change-chain output.
#     Before that it could show the split but not reproduce its consequence,
#     which verified only the half that already worked.
#
#     Generalised to BTC/DOGE/DASH/BCH later the same day (`STRANDED_FIXTURES`
#     in tauri-mocks.ts, address-driven so BTC needed no separate branch --
#     it shares LTC's esplora handler). DOGE/DASH/BCH also needed their FIRST
#     mock coverage of any kind: the header comment above once claimed "EVERY
#     chain" was mocked via http_proxy_call and that was true for LTC only --
#     check before trusting a coverage claim, don't just extend one.

# Which swap-engine stamp the mocked node reports, so the Settings card's
# engine states are reachable without a real runtime:
#   ok         (default) the engine matches this build
#   drift      an older engine is installed — renders the update note + button
#   unstamped  a hand-staged tree whose patch level cannot be read
#   none       nothing installed yet
# VITE_MOCK_ENGINE=drift
